, best by position","description":"Three quarterbacks who could go early? Big changes in the rankings? Mel Kiper Jr. stacks the best players on the 2027 draft board as of late November.","published":"2026-11-27T14:49:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50182998/2027-nfl-draft-rankings-kiper-big-board-top-prospects","type":"Story","byline":"Mel Kiper Jr.","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5126999/marquise-lightfoot","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marquise_Lightfoot"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Marquise Lightfoot","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marquise_Lightfoot","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-25T17:07:19Z","intro":"Marquise Lightfoot is an American college football defensive end for the Miami Hurricanes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Lightfoot attended Kenwood Academy in Chicago, Illinois. As a junior, he had 122 tackles and nine sacks. A five-star recruit, he was selected to play in the 2024 All-American Bowl. Lightfoot committed to the University of Miami to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at Miami in 2024, he played in nine games. As a sophomore in 2025, he appeared in all 16 games and made one start as a backup to Rueben Bain Jr. and Akheem Mesidor, recording 25 tackles and 2.5 sacks. Lightfoot returned to Miami for his junior season in 2026."}]}}